      "observed": "All VDD pins of FCC1 and NAVC1 are on unconnected nets, not tied to any 3.3V rail.",
      "expected": "VDD pins should be connected to the 3.3V rail (+3V3 or +3.3V) as stated in the specification.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"217\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"}
      ],
      "impact": "The MCUs receive no core power and will not operate; the board is completely non-functional.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "GND"],
      "observed": "PCA9685PW address pin A0 (pin 1) is tied to +3.3V, while A1–A5 are tied to GND.",
      "expected": "A0 should be tied to GND to set the I2C address to 0x40 as specified.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A0\") (pintype \"input\")) on net +3.3V"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"}
      ],
      "impact": "The PCA9685 responds at I2C address 0x41 instead of 0x40, so the FCC cannot control the PWM/servo outputs at the expected address.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["HSE1.1", "HSE1.3", "FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "HSE2.1", "HSE2.3", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "HSE1 is connected between FCC1 PE6 (pin 5) and PE7 (pin 37) instead of the HSE pins PH0/PH1. HSE2 is not connected to NAVC1 PH0/PH1 (pins 5/6); those pins instead have 2.2uF capacitors to GND.",
      "expected": "HSE1 should connect to FCC1 PH0 (pin 12) and PH1 (pin 13); HSE2 should connect to NAVC1 PH0 (pin 5) and PH1 (pin 6), with appropriate load capacitors.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"1\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"90\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0)\") (node (ref \"C37\") (pin \"1\")) (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | FCC / NAVC | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"}
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU receives a valid external clock from its crystal; the HSE oscillators will not start, forcing reliance on internal oscillators or causing complete clock failure.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple serious anomalies: both MCUs have unconnected VDD pins, the PCA9685 address pin A0 is tied high (changing its I2C address to 0x41), and the HSE crystals are miswired or disconnected from the MCU oscillator pins. These deviations would prevent the board from operating as specified."
}

